  m_text: Jake introduces a framework to help you choose the best-fit business model
    for your goals, lifestyle, skills, and experience. This chapter explains that
    every person has a different ideal business and helps you think through how involved
    you want to be before choosing your path.This chapter explains the difference
    between clients and customers. Customers usually buy lower-ticket self-serve
    products, while clients usually buy higher-ticket support, consulting, or services.
    You will learn how to choose between volume, depth, or a hybrid value ladder.This
    chapter explains the difference between clients and customers. Customers usually
    buy lower-ticket self-serve products, while clients usually buy higher-ticket
    support, consulting, or services. You will learn how to choose between volume,
    depth, or a hybrid value ladder.This chapter explains the difference between
    clients and customers. Customers usually buy lower-ticket self-serve products,
    while clients usually buy higher-ticket support, consulting, or services. You
    will learn how to choose between volume, depth, or a hybrid value ladder.This
    chapter explains the difference between clients and customers. Customers usually
    buy lower-ticket self-serve products, while clients usually buy higher-ticket
    support, consulting, or services. You will learn how to choose between volume,
